    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0197" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v10p1/pg163"/>

                <head>44. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="0" xml:id="d44-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-04-24">April 24,
                    1958</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>On 24 April, at the President’s direction, I advised Gen. Twining and Allen
                        Dulles that there are to be no reconnaissance flights, by
                    military or other aircraft, over the territory of the USSR or other Communist countries.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d44-f2"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">G.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d44-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d44-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Eisenhower Library, Project Clean Up, Intelligence Matters. No
                    classification marking. Prepared by Goodpaster.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d44-f2" n="1" xml:id="d44-f2-content">
                <p>In another memorandum for the record, dated April 24, Goodpaster wrote: “A.D. asked if OK to send a
                    man in by low-flying a/c. After checking I told him OK.” (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ibid</hi>.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
